0,Nilo-Saharan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilo-Saharan_languages,"The Nilo-Saharan languages are a proposed linguistic family consisting of around 210 Native African languages spoken by somewhere around 70 million speakers, mainly in the upper parts of the Chari and Nile rivers, including historic Nubia, north of where the two tributaries of the Nile meet.",Ma’di,Nilo-Saharan
